339263.literal_statement:
Let $C_n$ be a cycle of order $n=2k+x$, with $k\geq2$ and $1\leq x\leq2k-1$. The parameter $\lambda^k(C_n)$ is the largest number of labels in a labeling of the vertices that admits a packing of $k$ copies of $C_n$, with corresponding vertices receiving the same label. **Labeled packing conjecture for cycles.**

$$
\lambda^k(C_n)=
\begin{cases}
2,&\text{if }x=1\text{ and }k\text{ is even},\\
x+2,&\text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
$$

This conjecture concerns the remaining values of the labeled packing number for cycles after the results cited in the paper. The supplied context gives no resolution status.
